    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "description": "How to read this dashboard.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### External Secrets: how credentials reach the apps\n**What it does here.** One `ClusterSecretStore vault` (Kubernetes auth, role `external-secrets`) and one\n`ExternalSecret` per app (`kubectl --context k8s01 get externalsecrets -A`). Every hour (`refreshInterval: 1h`) the\ncontroller logs in to Vault, reads `secret/homelab/<name>` and writes the Kubernetes Secret. The **webhook** validates\nESO objects; the **cert-controller** keeps the webhook certificate and CRD conversion CA bundle valid.\n\n**Healthy looks like:** store READY, every ExternalSecret Ready (none NOT Ready), Vault UNSEALED, no provider errors,\nworkqueues at 0.\n\n**When something is red:** first look at *Vault seal status* — a sealed Vault is the usual cause (`docs/runbooks/vault.md`).\nThen `kubectl --context k8s01 describe externalsecret -n <ns> <name>` (wrong key/property?) and the controller logs\n(`kubectl --context k8s01 -n external-secrets logs deploy/external-secrets`). Force a refresh with the annotate command\nin `docs/runbooks/vault.md`. Note: after an ESO restart the per-ExternalSecret series reappear one by one as each object\nis reconciled (up to its refresh interval). Docs: [metrics & SLIs](https://external-secrets.io/latest/api/metrics/).",
        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Can the apps get their secrets?",
      "id": 2,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
